<title>USA: National Health sets no special dividend.</title>
<headline>National Health sets no special dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MURFREESBORO, Tenn. 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Health Investors Inc said because it increased its fourth quarter dividend to $0.74 per share from $0.70 per share, it would not declare a special dividend.</p>
<p>The company had previously said it might pay out a $0.10 to $0.15 per share special dividend.</p>
<p>&quot;We decided to increase the quarterly dividend by nearly six percent instead of paying a special dividend,&quot; said President Andy Adams.</p>
</text>
